    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Yordan Alvarez** (81.16) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98). **Yordan Alvarez** offers the highest floor, bolstered by a juicy matchup against Young (xERA 4.66) and an elite 0.477 xwOBA that justifies his UTIL slot. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our premier weapon for the scarce SB category; the combination of a favorable platoon edge against Matthews and a slow-working pitcher who allows for aggressive base-running makes him an absolute must-start. **Colt Keith** (68.51) and **Junior Caminero** (68.25) also provide high-efficiency output, benefiting from favorable SP skill metrics and premium spots in the order that maximize their counting stat potential.\n\nThe optimization process was tightest at the bottom of the outfield, where **Carson Benge** (54.69) narrowly edged out **Lars Nootbaar** (49.51) for the final spot. While **Lars Nootbaar** received a boost from Rodriguez\u2019s high xERA (4.82), his poor lineup placement at #8 and a negative platoon shift ultimately pushed him to the bench. Conversely, **Carson Benge** maintains a more consistent projected efficiency in a #5 hole. Caution is advised for **Trea Turner** (57.68) and **Kyle Schwarber** (55.89), as both face a stiff challenge in McLean (xERA 3.49); however, their base projections are strong enough to keep them in the starting lineup despite the increased risk of an efficiency dip. We continue to monitor the status of **Hyeseong Kim** and **Josh Smith** in the minors, alongside stash assets **Chase Meidroth**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez**, ensuring we remain ready for any roster volatility.",
